cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SLR Framework Studio
message: >-
  If you use this software in a published review, please cite it, and please
  state in your methods which parts of the review it carried out. The
  application generates an AI-use statement from its own log; it is written
  to be quoted.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kuldeep
    family-names: Verma
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7810-4796"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dr-kuldeep-verma/slr-framework-studio"
abstract: >-
  A desktop application that takes a systematic literature review from
  database exports to an evidence-graded theoretical framework, following
  PRISMA 2020. A language model makes a first pass at every judgement and a
  human confirms or overrides each one before it counts. Every decision
  stores the model, a hash of its prompt and input, its output and a
  timestamp in a hash-chained audit log, and every claim in every output
  traces to a stored record, page and quotation.
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - PRISMA
  - evidence synthesis
  - research software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
